    displayName: Sootwing
    species: pack-raven
    role: carrier
    source:
      type: folioSpread
      id: meadow-blooms
  - id: burr
    displayName: Burr
    species: meadow-vole
    role: gatherer
    source:
      type: almanacNode
      id: old-friend
  species:
  - id: meadow-vole
    displayName: Meadow vole
    roleLean: gatherer
    suggestedNames:
    - Bramble
    - Burr
    - Clover
    - Nettle
    - Sorrel
    - Pip
    - Thistle
    - Hazel
    trait:
      displayName: Meadow-forager
      description: +40% yield at berry and wildflower nodes
      kind: nodeYieldBonus
      value: 0.4
      resources:
      - berries
      - wildflowers
    minMigration: 0
    inscriptions:
    - Knows my step now. Doesn't look up.
    - Found the last ripe cane in the rain, and left me half.
    - Third season she has found me. I have stopped calling it luck.
  - id: red-squirrel
    displayName: Red squirrel
    roleLean: gatherer
    suggestedNames:
    - Cob
    - Filbert
    - Russet
    - Brindle
    - Scamper
    trait:
      displayName: Mast-hoarder
      description: +40% yield at nut and mushroom nodes
      kind: nodeYieldBonus
      value: 0.4
      resources:
      - nuts
      - mushrooms
    minMigration: 0
    inscriptions:
    - Buries more than he digs up. The wood is in his debt.
    - Showed me a cache I never taught him. I think it was a gift.
    - Old now, and still burying. No winter has caught him short.
  - id: sedge-linnet
    displayName: Sedge linnet
    roleLean: gatherer
    suggestedNames:
    - Trill
    - Reedling
    - Fife
    - Sol
    - Wren
    trait:
      displayName: Nest-weaver
      description: +40% yield at fibre and reed nodes
      kind: nodeYieldBonus
      value: 0.4
      resources:
      - fibres
      - reeds
    minMigration: 0
    inscriptions:
    - Pulls the year's best grasses first, and sings over the work.
    - Wove a strand of my rope into her nest. I take that as a wage.
    - The reeds bend before she lands now. They know her.
  - id: bramble-hare
    displayName: Bramble hare
    roleLean: gatherer
    suggestedNames:
    - Loper
    - Switch
    - Fleet
    - Bracken
    - Clove
    trait:
      displayName: Hedge-browser
      description: +40% yield at herb and rare-herb nodes
      kind: nodeYieldBonus
      value: 0.4
      resources:
      - herbs
      - rare-herbs
    minMigration: 0
    inscriptions:
    - Tastes the hedge for what's ripe. Leaves my mistakes on the stem.
    - Steered me round the thorn patch by sitting still in front of it.
    - The hedge opens for her. I have seen it, and I won't argue.
  - id: warren-weasel
    displayName: Warren weasel
    roleLean: gatherer
    suggestedNames:
    - Slink
    - Sable
    - Nip
    - Vein
    - Ferro
    trait:
      displayName: Ore-tunneler
      description: +40% yield at copper scree and tin seam nodes
      kind: nodeYieldBonus
      value: 0.4
      resources:
      - copper-scree
      - tin-seam
    minMigration: 0
    inscriptions:
    - Follows the seam like a burrow. Comes up dusted green.
    - Taps the stone twice where it's worth my while. Twice, always.
    - The hill lets him through. I dig where he tells me now.
  - id: furrow-hedgehog
    displayName: Furrow hedgehog
    roleLean: gatherer
    suggestedNames:
    - Quill
    - Snuffle
    - Prickle
    - Furze
    - Tumble
    trait:
      displayName: Earth-rooter
      description: +40% yield at clay and iron gravel nodes
      kind: nodeYieldBonus
      value: 0.4
      resources:
      - clay
      - iron-gravel
    minMigration: 0
    inscriptions:
    - Roots the wet ground, and huffs when it's good.
    - Sleeps in the clay pit as if the ground had been warmed for him.
    - The earth gives him what it hides from my spade.
  - id: tawny-owl
    displayName: Tawny owl
    roleLean: gatherer
    suggestedNames:
    - Hoot
    - Umber
    - Hush
    - Grey
    - Willow
    trait:
      displayName: Grove-and-river hunter
      description: +40% yield at timber and fishing nodes
      kind: nodeYieldBonus
      value: 0.4
      resources:
      - timber
      - fish
    minMigration: 0
    inscriptions:
    - Works the wood's edge and the shallows, and judges my knots.
    - Left a trout at my feet at dusk. No comment offered.
    - The river and the wood have settled which one owns her. Neither.
  - id: osier-otter
    displayName: Osier otter
    roleLean: gatherer
    suggestedNames:
    - Rill
    - Wade
    - Tarn
    - Eddy
    - Slick
    trait:
      displayName: Fen-swimmer
      description: +40% yield at peat and glow-moss nodes
      kind: nodeYieldBonus
      value: 0.4
      resources:
      - peat
      - glow-moss
    minMigration: 0
    inscriptions:
    - Works the wet margins as if the water owed him.
    - Brought the moss up glowing and dry. I no longer ask how.
    - The fen holds its breath around him. He has never once noticed.
  - id: horseshoe-bat
    displayName: Horseshoe bat
    roleLean: gatherer
    suggestedNames:
    - Vesper
    - Bell
    - Dusk
    - Flit
    - Ping
    trait:
      displayName: Dark-delver
      description: +40% yield at deep ore and crystal nodes
      kind: nodeYieldBonus
      value: 0.4
      resources:
      - deep-ores
      - crystals
    minMigration: 0
    inscriptions:
    - Hangs over the lamp while I work. I have decided this is company.
    - Found the seam by singing at it. The stone sang back.
    - The dark is her country and she its keeper. Nothing below moves unannounced.
  - id: ermine
    displayName: Ermine
    roleLean: gatherer
    suggestedNames:
    - Drift
    - Pale
    - Frost
    - Silk
    - Winter
    trait:
      displayName: Winter-walker
      description: +40% yield at ashglass and glacier ice nodes
      kind: nodeYieldBonus
      value: 0.4
      resources:
      - ashglass
      - glacier-ice
    minMigration: 0
    inscriptions:
    - White as the glass he digs. The ash does not stick to him.
    - Circled the pit all night. No other track comes near it.
    - He wears the old winter like it was fitted. Perhaps it was.
  - id: kea
    displayName: Kea
    roleLean: gatherer
    suggestedNames:
    - Kee
    - Scoria
    - Sleet
    - Rascal
    - Vane
    trait:
      displayName: Flock-rider
      description: +40% yield at egg and wool nodes
      kind: nodeYieldBonus
      value: 0.4
      resources:
      - eggs
      - wool
    minMigration: 0
    inscriptions:
    - Undid the strap I tied twice, and left the buckle where I'd find it. A fee,
      I think.
    - Rides the ewes down the slope for the joy of it. The flock has voted to allow
      this.
    - The wind is his and he lends it. Nothing on this mountain is closed to him
      now.
  - id: pika
    displayName: Pika
    roleLean: gatherer
    suggestedNames:
    - Mow
    - Posy
    - Stack
    - Whin
    - Cairn
    trait:
      displayName: Hay-piler
      description: +40% yield at lichen and sky-blossom nodes
      kind: nodeYieldBonus
      value: 0.4
      resources:
      - lichen
      - sky-blossoms
    minMigration: 0
    inscriptions:
    - Cuts her hay in the sun hours and stacks it under the one dry stone. I have
      started copying her.
    - Whistles the hawk's arrival before the hawk. The whole slope moves on her word.
    - Her winter is stacked and dried by midsummer. The cold arrives and finds it
      owes her.
  - id: pack-raven
    displayName: Pack raven
    roleLean: carrier
    suggestedNames:
    - Sootwing
    - Corvus
    - Jet
    - Rook
    - Ash
    - Grackle
    - Cinder
    - Onyx
    trait:
      displayName: Deep pockets
      description: "Windfall bubbles pay +25% more while she walks \u2014 she fetches
        them home"
      kind: bubbleRewardBonus
      value: 0.25
      resources: []
    minMigration: 0
    inscriptions:
    - Carries more than looks possible, and counts every piece.
    - Took the long way round the storm and set down nothing.
    - I have stopped checking the loads. Her idea, somehow.
  - id: fell-pony
    displayName: Fell pony
    roleLean: carrier
    suggestedNames:
    - Moss
    - Bracken
    - Tor
    - Gale
    - Pennine
    trait:
      displayName: Half-broke
      description: "Carries what the warden picks, so their hands never leave the
        work \u2014 the warden's own gathering +50%"
      kind: wardenYieldBonus
      value: 0.5
      resources: []
    minMigration: 0
    inscriptions:
    - Came down off the fell on her own account and has stayed on it.
    - Will take the panniers. Will not take the halter twice.
    - Ten winters of her own weather in her. I lead her nowhere; we go the same way.
