  dialogue:
    waystones:
    - key: sunfield-meadow
      text: Walk gently. The meadow fed them, too, and they are under it.
    - key: bramble-hedgerows
      text: The stone does not grow back. Take it like you mean it.
    - key: old-growth-wood
      text: These roots drink deeper than you will ever dig. Let them.
    - key: silverrun-river
      text: The river keeps no ledger. Count what you take, for it will not.
    - key: mistfen-marsh
      text: The fen remembers every weight it has carried. Step lightly; it is counting.
    - key: the-hollows
      text: The dark below was not always empty. Leave it the quiet it paid for.
    - key: highland-crags
      text: Others folded flocks on this height, and the wind has their names. Count
        yours home each night.
    - key: cloudreach-peaks
      text: "You have come to the end of the walking. What is left we said a stone
        at a time \u2014 come back each season, and hear it out."
    verses:
    - key: sunfield-meadow
      text: What you carry is borrowed. Set some down, and see what follows you home.
    - key: bramble-hedgerows
      text: Sweetness kept, stone made bright. Show the hedge what the taking taught
        you.
    - key: old-growth-wood
      text: Wood made useful, and one bone of what came before. The grove would hold
        it again.
    - key: silverrun-river
      text: Of all you pulled from the water, the river asks the finest back. It
        knows you have it.
    - key: mistfen-marsh
      text: Brew what the still water grew, and pour a little back where the lights
        gather.
    - key: the-hollows
      text: Ore made bright, and the glass the burning left. Carry the deep's own
        wealth back down.
    - key: highland-crags
      text: What the flock gives freely, give on. The warmth was never yours to keep.
    - key: cloudreach-peaks
      text: Flower and ice, and the cordial that holds them both. Pour it out on
        ground that grows nothing, and ask for nothing back.
    provisioner:
    - id: prov-01
      trigger: first-visit
      line: Sell me nothing you would weep to lose. I do not give refunds, and the
        land does not either.
    - id: prov-02
      trigger: after-migration
      line: The last warden asked fewer questions. Hm. Perhaps that was the trouble.
    migrationVignette:
    - The camp folds. The land exhales.
    - What you gave, it keeps.
    insectPlates:
    - key: stags-herald
      text: Antlers on a beetle no longer than your thumb. It fought something once,
        or meant to. The drawing is all I keep; the meadow keeps the rest.
    - key: silver-skimmer
      text: It held the one reach of river all afternoon and let me sketch it, wings
        still. The river fed its kind ten thousand years. I gave the page my hand
        and gave the water back its guest.
    - key: those-who-sow
      text: They carry the flowers from field to field without being asked, and have
        longer than we have. Whoever tends this place, it is not only us. I drew
        them, and let them go on.
    - key: lantern-bearers
      text: They light the drowned paths every night, for no one. I was never the
        reason, and I may still be grateful. Four evenings of drawing, and not one
        lantern paused for me.
    - key: quiet-court
      text: They sing in galleries no light has ever reached, to no audience at all.
        Five evenings by lamplight, drawing what has never been seen. They did not
        stop singing once.
    - key: parchment-wings
      text: Wings thin as the pages I draw them on, and they fly only while the sun
        holds. Four afternoons of sun, this high, in this wind. I owed the mountain
        every one.
    - key: windborne
      text: Nothing hatched up here. The wind carries them to the summit and sets
        them down, and what lives on the rock lives on that. Four days drawing the
        ones still whole. They were going somewhere else.
    - key: wayfarers-plate
      text: A loose leaf, folded twice, left in a place I would pass. Another hand
        drew it, steadier than mine and long gone. I did not walk for this one. It
        is in the book now, and I am still walking.
    finalWaystones:
      zoneId: cloudreach-peaks
      stones:
      - key: the-rows
        text: From this height the old fields are still in rows. We cut them straight,
          and we called it tending.
      - key: the-debt
        text: The giving slowed and we did not stop, because we had been careful,
          and careful felt like credit. The sky closed for a hundred years and settled
          it.
      - key: the-few
        text: The few who came down after planted nothing they would live to sit
          under. You keep their rule, and you have their hands.
      - key: the-ground
        text: Nothing is kept up here for you to collect, and no one is waiting to
          forgive it. Go down and put something in the ground.
